+### The epoch-2 discard bridge
+
+The separately built discard bridge uses the normal preserving epoch-2 to
+epoch-2 update. It does not change the native executable, retained registration,
+or reporting contract. It handles only the pre-session request described in
+[Discard a failed request before session creation](session-preparations.md#discard-a-failed-request-before-session-creation).
+Do not select it to recover a running or materialized session.
+
+Keep the exact bridge build selected until it confirms cleanup of the original
+request. Profile preparation, validation and activation refuse while the marker
+exists, even after the original records have moved. If unlink succeeded but the
+marker directory sync was not confirmed, those commands can admit a transition.
+Admission and the saved `cancelled` mapping do not confirm cleanup. Resume only
+with the same verified startup grant. Do not roll back to an older reader,
+retry creation, or remove the marker to force an update.
+
+For an administratively scheduled discard, select the bridge with no grant
+present. Verify that the stock transition finished and the new portal replaced
+its predecessor. An independently authenticated machine administrator can
+then schedule the one exact original request and restart only that portal.
+The portal checks the root-owned grant, selected package, registered service
+and retained typed machine claim before it discards anything. An unconfirmed
+startup stops without repeating the operation. Keep the same bridge and claim
+while it is held, and do not start an update to recover it.
+
+Completion leaves only the ordinary terminal preparation mapping in the live
+inventory. For a scheduled discard, also verify the original audit and marker
+cleanup, then have the administrator retire the same grant. An absent grant or
+an active systemd unit does not establish completion. Verify that the next
+package understands the mapping and cannot replay the retired request before
+preparing the next ordinary switch.
